==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛləʊ/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛləʊ}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈbɛloʊ/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛloʊ}}
*: {{audio|en-us-bellow.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} [[belwen]], from {{etyl|ang}} [[bylgian]], cognate with [[belg]] “leather bag,” [[bellan]] “to roar,” [[blawan|blāwan]] “to blow”. Cognate with German {{term|bellen||to bark}}, Old Slavonic {{term|блея}}<ref>{{R:Webster 1913|bellow}}</ref> (Russian {{term|блеять||baa, bleat}}).

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{examples-right|examples={{audio|Elkbellow.ogg|The bellow of an [[elk]]}}}}

# the deep [[roar]] of a large animal, or any similar loud noise

